      "question_id": "Q2",
      "question": "Which internal roles are required to attend the vendor meeting, and who is responsible for setting and distributing the agenda beforehand?",
      "answer": "The equipment engineer and meeting organizer are the key internal roles involved. The equipment engineer prepares the agenda and issue summary before the meeting. The manager and action-item owner are involved post-meeting. Mandatory attendance requirements beyond these roles are not specified."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q3",
      "question": "In what format is the meeting discussion captured — for example, a structured template, free-text notes, or a recording — and where is that output stored after the meeting?",
      "answer": "The meeting organizer records decisions and open questions during the meeting, producing meeting minutes. These are stored in a shared document repository. The specific capture format — structured template, free-text, or recording — is not specified."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q4",
      "question": "How are action items identified from the meeting output — does one designated person extract them manually, or is there a defined process or template that guides what qualifies as an action item?",
      "answer": "The meeting organizer records decisions and open questions, from which the manager then assigns action-item owners and due dates. This suggests a manual extraction process led by the organizer and manager. A defined template or criteria for what qualifies as an action item is not specified."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q5",
      "question": "What tool or system is used to track action items after they are assigned, and is there a standard deadline or response window that applies to each item?",
      "answer": "Action items are tracked using an action-item tracker. Due dates are assigned per item by the manager, so deadlines are item-specific rather than governed by a single standard response window. Whether a default deadline window exists is not specified."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q6",
      "question": "What criteria must be met for an action item to be considered closed, and what happens if an item is not resolved within the expected timeframe — is there a defined escalation path?",
      "answer": "A missed follow-up deadline is listed as a recognized exception, implying it requires handling. However, specific closure criteria and a formal escalation path are not specified in the workflow. The action-item owner is responsible for tracking progress toward resolution."
    }
  ]
